From 3329a918a96f91911201002d557e120ee5bc6b07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qr0n <77075118+qr0n@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 07:11:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] CUDA: GP100: fold the recurrent-state plumbing of gated
 delta-net layers into their kernels

At decode, every linear-attention (gated delta-net) layer of qwen35 ran a string of tiny kernels whose only job
was to move state or apply one elementwise op: a GET_ROWS copy of the ~1.5 MB/card recurrent state, GET_ROWS +
CONCAT + CPY around the 1-D conv, two l2_norms, a bias ADD, a sigmoid, and a separate rms_norm, gate multiply and
fp16 activation conversion around the output projection. On GP100 each costs 2-9 us of mostly launch latency.
This folds them into the kernels that already read the data (sm_60 only, one sequence):

- gated_delta_net reads the recurrent state in place from the cache row (the GET_ROWS copy is skipped);
- ssm_conv reads its cached window in place and writes the shifted window back (GET_ROWS/CONCAT/CPY skipped);
- gated_delta_net applies the q/k l2_norm and the beta sigmoid itself;
- ADD(alpha, dt) -> SOFTPLUS -> MUL(A) runs as one kernel;
- the gated head norm silu(z) * rms_norm(x) * w also fills the fp16 activation cache for the output projection.

Every fused result is bit-identical (same float ops, same reduction order): decode-path KLD against a Q8_0
reference is unchanged in every digit (0.011261, top-1 94.686%). Matching is stateless and use-count exact, and
every read deferred past a tensor's last graph consumer is proven not clobbered by ggml-alloc buffer reuse at
match time -- an earlier version without that check was fast and wrong (KLD 0.0855). When any check fails the
stock nodes run. Kill switch: GGML_CUDA_GP100_STATE_DISABLE=1.

qwen3.8-27b UD-Q4_K_XL, 2x P100, -sm tensor: 1786 -> 1306 kernel launches/token, tg128 33.69 -> 36.31 (+7.8%),
real-use aggregate (6 prompts x 2 seeds, temp 0.6, via llama-server) 32.30 -> 35.25 (+9.1%, uniform across prompts
up to 11k context), pp512 unchanged. Other architectures: pre-existing kernels byte-identical on sm_61/sm_75.

Also carries the Q6_K output-head R=8 row mapping (nrows >= 32768), which measured null (-0.2%, within noise); it
is included so that this patch reproduces the tested tree exactly.

